WEBVTT

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.500
Let's finish with the tasks

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.620
you'll use, not

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:04.100
just the lessons you've watched.

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:05.560
Open your workbook

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.220
and mark each relevant task

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:09.360
as independent, needs coaching,

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.520
blocked by setup or access,

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:12.820
or not your role.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:14.540
For a salesperson,

00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:15.610
check that you can

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:16.660
use the right account,

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.600
confirm Facebook and inventory,

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:20.100
select a vehicle,

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:21.200
read the Queue,

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:22.980
review listing changes

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.640
and answer a buyer's question.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:26.770
If you use Auto-Pilot,

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:27.910
explain what needs

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:29.280
to stay running and where

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.300
you check its state.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.580
For an individual account owner,

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:34.750
include feed setup, listing

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:36.120
wording and the difference

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.140
between your posting

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.730
allowance and AI credits.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:40.270
For a manager,

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:41.770
include team access,

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:43.550
the correct reporting period

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.650
and one practical coaching task.

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:48.090
A manager-only user doesn't

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:49.260
need to publish a vehicle

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:50.500
to complete their training.

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:52.130
Pick one task you

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:53.400
want to improve and replay

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.420
that lesson.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:56.000
Product Tour is at the

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.420
bottom left of the AutoLander

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:58.720
sidebar if you need

00:00:58.720 --> 00:00:59.830
help finding the screen.

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:01.810
Then try a different

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:03.250
example and see whether

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:04.670
you can explain and locate

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:05.930
the step without help.

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:07.450
If a setup issue

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:08.470
is still open,

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:09.590
write down who is

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:11.290
helping and what happens next.

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:12.940
You don't need to buy,

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:14.540
post or delete something

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:16.080
just to finish the workbook.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:17.690
Bring the same checks

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:18.950
into your next working day,

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:20.730
and build confidence one

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:22.510
successful task at a time.
